  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substitution gives \\(a+b=4+(-4)=0.\\) Hence the expression becomes \\(\\frac{3}{0},\\) which is undefined.\n\nThus, the expression is meaningless and the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute the two given values into the denominator first",
        "A fraction with denominator \\(0\\) is undefined"
